## 3. Codebase Analysis & Strategic Guidance

The following analysis is based on my direct review of the current codebase. Use these notes and tips to guide your implementation.

### Relevant Existing Code
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/modules/orders/views/OrdersDashboard.vue`
    *   **Summary:** Full admin orders view already lives under the modular path. It renders stats cards, filters, a `OrdersTable` listing, bulk-action flows, and an `OrderDetailPanel` drawer wired to `useOrdersStore`, telemetry hooks, tenant feature flag checks, and PrimeVue toasts.
    *   **Recommendation:** Extend or refactor this view rather than duplicating a new `/src/views/OrdersView.vue`. Keep the screen responsive (`@apply` Tailwind classes), maintain ARIA/live-region cues, and reuse injected components (`OrdersTable`, `BulkUpdateModal`, `OrderDetailPanel`) when adding timeline badges, inline capture/refund actions, or additional cards.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/modules/orders/store.ts`
    *   **Summary:** Pinia store backing the dashboard; owns order list, stats, filters, pagination, selection set, SSE wiring, and exposes actions for CRUD events (`loadOrders`, `updateOrderStatus`, `bulkUpdateStatus`, `exportOrdersCSV`, etc.). Emits telemetry on major mutations.
    *   **Recommendation:** Introduce any new client state (e.g., refund dialog visibility, audit timeline data) here so multiple components stay in sync. Follow the existing error handling pattern (set `error`, throw for caller) and reuse SSE handlers to refresh stats/timelines when statuses change. When adding unit tests, copy the structure seen in `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/stores/__tests__/catalog.spec.ts` (mock `apiClient`, assert telemetry invocations, and validate optimistic behavior).
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/modules/orders/api.ts`
    *   **Summary:** Typed API layer for orders endpoints plus an SSE connector. Functions already cover list, detail, stats, status update, cancellation, refund, bulk update, and CSV export operations, returning typed DTOs defined in `types.ts`.
    *   **Recommendation:** Consume these helpers inside the store/handlers instead of duplicating fetch logic. If new endpoints exist in the spec (e.g., capture payment intent, attach internal notes, audit timeline feed), add matching helper functions here and re-export from the store so the view stays declarative.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/router/index.ts`
    *   **Summary:** Root router registers shared layout routes and dynamically merges module route arrays. `ordersRoutes` currently point to `modules/orders/views/OrdersDashboard.vue` and enforce feature flags/RBAC.
    *   **Recommendation:** Any new order detail routes or nested components must be added through `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/modules/orders/routes.ts` so the router import list remains the single source of truth. Preserve `meta` keys (`requiresAuth`, `requiredRole`, `featureFlag`, `title`) because guards enforce authentication, feature toggles, and impersonation safety.

### Implementation Tips & Notes
*   **Tip:** Paths in the planning docs reference `src/main/webui/...`, but the actual SPA lives under `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui`. Keep new components (e.g., `OrderTimeline.vue`, `RefundDialog.vue`) inside `modules/orders/components` or `modules/orders/views` to align with the current module boundary and router wiring.
*   **Tip:** Reuse shared composables (`useI18n`, `useAuthStore`, `useTenantStore`, `useToast`, `emitTelemetryEvent`) exactly as shown in `OrdersDashboard.vue` so RBAC, feature flags, impersonation banners, and audit logs remain consistent. Avoid direct API calls from components; go through `useOrdersStore` actions.
*   **Tip:** PrimeVue + Tailwind are the default UI stack. Components import PrimeVue widgets (Sidebar, Button, Tag) alongside Tailwind utility classes defined via `@apply`. Follow this pattern for new dialogs/timelines so theme tokens from the design system apply correctly.
*   **Tip:** The store already exposes SSE management—call `connectSSE()`/`disconnectSSE()` from lifecycle hooks and update timeline components whenever SSE events touch the selected order. Emit screen-reader live-region updates (see `liveRegionMessage`) whenever you perform asynchronous actions like refunds or captures.
*   **Tip:** Unit tests should live under `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/modules/orders/__tests__/` (create this folder if missing) and can mirror the catalog store tests: mock the API module, assert state transitions, and verify that optimistic UI flows (filters, pagination, SSE) behave as acceptance criteria require.
*   **Tip:** Keep audit history requirements in mind—`OrderDetailPanel.vue` already renders a simple timeline list. If you need a richer `OrderTimeline` component (attachments, actor badges), build it as a reusable component fed by `order.timeline` entries and plug it into the drawer so the operational “inspect order timeline entries” control is satisfied.
